{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Just stones.</b> These are the weights that one weighs against." "<b>The ephah.</b> It is the dry measure." "<b>And the hin.</b> This is the liquid measure." "<b>Who brought you out.</b> On this condition. Another interpretation: I distinguished in Egypt between the drop of a firstborn and the drop that is not of a firstborn, and I am faithful to exact punishment from one who buries his weights in salt to defraud creatures who do not recognize them (Bava Metzia 61a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:20.967159706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}